<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA rice export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales of 18,600 MT were down 51 percent from the week earlier and 36 percent below the 4-week average.</p>
<p>Colombia (10,000 MT--all rough) was the primary buyer, with smaller quantities to Saudi Arabia (2,500 MT), Mexico (2,300 MT--all rough), Barbados (1,500 MT), El Salvador (1,400 MT--all rough), Belgium (1,300 MT), Canada (1,200 MT), and Honduras (1,100 MT).  Decreases were reported for Haiti (2,800 MT) and Guatemala (1,500 MT--all rough).</p>
<p>Exports of 31,000 MT were 37 percent below the week earlier and 43 percent under the 4-week average.  The major destinations were Guatemala (9,300 MT), Mexico (7,000 MT), and Turkey (5,800 MT).</p>
</text>
